{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact BR-12 head 2d65246837bd78b0b60d2f31c4baa68b74f9e604 on builder/br12-test-trims-20261108, tree 924a742a, all eleven artifacts on the paths that differ from RoomOpening head 035a784e, under builder promise 7498ea3f for review request f7ce2fce. That includes the apps/sandbox/worker.ts seal. Three slow tests now run at controlled boundaries. Production defaults, stored formats and recorded meaning are unchanged.\n\nThe changes:\n\n- The sandbox.\n  - apps/sandbox/worker.ts `fetch` gains a fourth parameter, `replySeconds = REPLY_SECONDS`, and uses it in the three `within` windows.\n  - The Workers runtime passes three arguments, so production keeps 30 seconds.\n  - The late-headers test now passes 0.02 seconds instead of waiting 30, and keeps its 503, background and release-gated checks.\n- Custody.\n  - `CustodyStore` gains an optional `unresolvedMost`, and both admission checks read `store.unresolvedMost ?? UNRESOLVED_MOST`.\n  - `sqliteStore` sets it from its bounds, defaulting to `UNRESOLVED_MOST`. The production bounds do not set it.\n  - The hosted H6 matrix now crosses an injected count of 2 through the real endpoint.\n  - A new SQLite case witnesses the real default directly. It asserts that the count is 256, refuses the 257th record before any envelope is built, and admits the 257th after one record settles. It also shows the smaller configured count refusing.\n- HTTP. http.test.ts replaces fixed sleeps and polling with awaited events: configuration entry, stream text and stream state. One polled check, \"the opening holds its snapshot\", becomes `await paused.entered()`, which waits for the configuration read to reach the hold. The precondition is the same. If it is never met, the test now times out instead of failing an assertion. Every other assertion maps one to one: the file goes from 83 to 82 assertions and keeps its 10 cases.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The seal. I recomputed apps/sandbox/worker.ts outside the builder's worktree with the security test's parser. Main gives the old literal 3208f16c…, and the head gives the new literal 6554155e…. Only that literal and its comment change in scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs.\n- The control. With the configured count ignored, only the new SQLite case fails, by assertion at sqlite-custody.test.ts:110. The other cases pass, and the source is restored.\n- The gate. I read gate.exit at the shared top head 5364d494: \"exit 0\". The log ends \"gate passed\", and before.json and after.json are byte-equal. After the gate, only the two notes and the shared gate manifest change.\n- The Page module. Page workflow run 42558851410 passed at 99092048 on this stack. Later commits change only notes and manifests.\n- The evidence. The BR-12 manifest hashes to 6bdfc9af…, the value that the request cites. Its 35 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match. The shared gate manifest f7a94a2a… is checked under my RoomOpening approval 5ec6d8ac.\n- Scope. RoomOpening 035a784e is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against that lower head, the head changes exactly the eleven artifact paths. The commit-message check from main passes: 17 checked, 0 flagged.\n\nLand in order, as ruling c5c24191 requires: RoomOpening first, then BR-12. Check the BR-12 merge plan against main after RoomOpening lands.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Each bound is now an injected value with the production constant as its default, at the owner that enforces it.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The sandbox's reply window cannot be changed by a request, because the runtime passes no fourth argument. The custody count stays at 256 unless a store's bounds set another value, and no production bounds do. Both admission paths still refuse before an envelope is signed.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One note: `unresolvedMost` has no upper clamp, so a future store could raise the count above the production bound. Clamping it to `UNRESOLVED_MOST` would keep that bound absolute.\n\nThis approval authorizes no deployment and closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:216921b122be297c0f9a3087ea5e18332a8e47cf","binding":"assigned","head":"2d65246837bd78b0b60d2f31c4baa68b74f9e604","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1af8598cf3b8a1dccf4d76aa105f35adfae2f5dc\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7498ea3f880fa830607fa8b64131c9f0c6bb6f27\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1af8598cf3b8a1dccf4d76aa105f35adfae2f5dc","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}